Subject: [RFC PATCH] clk: mediatek: accept the MT6991 pextp compatible on mt8196-pextp

The boot device tree comes from the vendor image and spells the PCIe
transmit PHY clock blocks as "mediatek,mt6991-pextp0cfg_ao" (underscore).
The shared driver only matches the mt8196 hyphen form, so the provider
never binds, the PCIe PHY keeps deferring on its ref/mcu clocks and
PCIe0 never enumerates. The clock IDs are identical (PEXTP_REF=3,
MCU_BUS=2), so accept both spellings.

--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8196-pextp.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8196-pextp.c
@@ -111,6 +111,9 @@
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_match_clk_mt8196_pextp[] = {
+	/* The vendor device tree spells the same blocks with underscores. */
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6991-pextp0cfg_ao", .data = &pext_mcd },
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6991-pextp1cfg_ao", .data = &pext1_mcd },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8196-pextp0cfg-ao", .data = &pext_mcd },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8196-pextp1cfg-ao", .data = &pext1_mcd },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
